The existing [asset writer](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/apps/mischief/scripts/emit-assets.ts) emits output identified by a hash of its content.
The Worker reads that output through [static assets](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/apps/mischief/src/static-assets.ts).

The [code-snippets design brief](/lore/code-snippets) keeps Git reads and highlighting in build-time work.
Request-time work receives static output.
It does not resolve Git objects or start Shiki.

The proposed check verifies that neither the snippet package nor Shiki enters the startup bundle.
The existing [startup budget](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/apps/mischief/scripts/startup-budget.ts) limits:
- Entry JavaScript to 3,300,000 bytes.
- Complete JavaScript upload to 5,000,000 bytes.

Check the modules included in the bundle, as well as its size, to verify which packages it includes.

[Checks before writing output](/lore/accumulate-independent-errors) finish before assets are written.
[Pinned sources](/lore/pinned-sources-can-report-drift) require no generation-time network fetch.

See [the glossary](/glossary) for build-time work and request-time work.
